title: Belts that carry piles
intro: A Conveyor with a Spacing carries several items to a cell, gliding a set distance apart and piling up at a full machine, with a line passing under it.

project: Empty | Piles

chapter: The belt | Several items to a cell
create: Empty
rename: Line
add: Conveyor
set: Conveyor.Belts = -4 0 right\n-3 0 right\n-2 0 right\n-1 0 right under\n0 0 right\n1 0 right\n2 0 right\n3 0 right\n-1 -2 down\n-1 -1 down\n-1 1 down\n-1 2 down
explain: field:Conveyor.Belts | Belts | A belt runs right along row zero. The cell in the middle is an under cell: the line coming down column minus one passes beneath it.
set: Conveyor.Spacing = 0.25
explain: field:Conveyor.Spacing | Spacing | With a spacing of a quarter cell, items glide on four to a cell instead of one, each a quarter cell behind the one ahead.
set: Conveyor.Speed = 2
set: Conveyor.MovingArrows = true
explain: field:Conveyor.MovingArrows | Moving Arrows | The belt's arrows slide along with the items, so it looks like it moves, and stop when the line stops.
look: 0, 0, 5

chapter: Machines | A maker, a reader with a table of four, and a box line
deselect
create: Empty
rename: Maker
set: Transform.Position.X = -5
add: Inventory
set: Inventory.Items = Deck
editorset: Inventory.Items:count:1 = 12
add: ConveyorPort
set: ConveyorPort.Kind = Out
explain: component:ConveyorPort | Conveyor Port | The maker's Out port puts its twelve decks on the belt as fast as there's room.
deselect
create: Empty
rename: Reader
set: Transform.Position.X = 4
add: Inventory
add: ConveyorPort
set: ConveyorPort.Items = Deck
set: ConveyorPort.Holds = 4
explain: field:ConveyorPort.Holds | Holds | The reader takes decks until its table holds four. The rest pile up on the belt behind it.
deselect
create: Empty
rename: Boxes
set: Transform.Position = -1, 3, 0
add: Inventory
set: Inventory.Items = Box
editorset: Inventory.Items:count:1 = 8
add: ConveyorPort
set: ConveyorPort.Kind = Out
deselect
create: Empty
rename: Box Bin
set: Transform.Position = -1, -3, 0
add: ConveyorPort
explain: component:ConveyorPort | Conveyor Port | Boxes go down the column, under the belt, into a bin that takes everything.

chapter: Play | Gliding, passing under, piling up
play
wait: 4
say: Decks glide along a quarter cell apart while boxes pass under the belt, neither line waiting for the other.
wait: 5
expectvalue: Reader.Inventory.Items = Deck 4
expectvalue: Reader.ConveyorPort.Blocked = true
say: The reader's table is full, so the decks behind it bunch up into a pile, packed a quarter cell apart.
stop
say: A splitter's Filters send named items one way and the rest another, a full loop keeps going round, and Belt Tiles moves painted belt art with the items.
